#------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LaTe3 at 100 K -- AVERAGE (unmodulated) structure
#
# Source: ja0641608_si_002.cif, data block "data_LaTe3" (100.0(3) K),
#         supporting information of J. Am. Chem. Soc. article ja0641608.
#
# The source refines LaTe3 at 100 K as an incommensurately modulated (CDW)
# structure in superspace group C2cm(00g)000. This file keeps the average
# structure only: the 8 superspace operations with the 4th coordinate (x4)
# dropped, i.e. 3D space group C2cm (non-standard setting), and the average
# atom positions. The modulation is NOT applied here; it is recorded below
# for reference. Use the source file for the full modulated refinement.
#
# CDW wave vector:  q = (0, 0, 0.2757(4)) in units of c*
# Displacive modulation, first harmonic (fractional units; u = cos*cos(2pi x4) + sin*sin(2pi x4)):
#   atom  axis      cos            sin
#   La1   x       0.0059(2)      0
#   La1   y      -0.00003(14)    0
#   La1   z       0              0.0008(8)
#   Te1   x       0.0008(2)      0
#   Te1   y       0.00006(17)    0
#   Te1   z       0             -0.0008(9)
#   Te2   x      -0.0325(5)      0
#   Te2   y      -0.00167(14)    0
#   Te2   z       0             -0.0046(10)
#   Te3   x       0.0236(4)      0
#   Te3   y       0.00008(15)    0
#   Te3   z       0             -0.0011(10)
# (Te2 x amplitude ~ 0.0325*a = 0.14 A; Te3 x ~ 0.0236*a = 0.10 A.)
#
# Stacking (van der Waals) axis: b.
#------------------------------------------------------------------------------

